#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0329 expect=violation domain=TE
#note "AUTHORED BY Plan B phase 4d as the direction pin for -skipped_all_columns_absent-TE, and the arm CDISC-CG0329's own sheet row is written about (Variable TEDUR, Condition TEENRL = null, Rule TEDUR ^= null). TEENRL is not present in the dataset at all and TEDUR is empty on row 2 -> that element has neither an end rule nor a planned duration, so the 'TEENRL not_exists' disjunct folds true while the TEDUR half stays UNKNOWN under BroadcastFold (the column is present) and the row loop decides -- one finding on row 2 only. UNCHANGED by Plan B phase 4d: Requirements.Variables.Any [TEENRL, TEDUR] is satisfied because TEDUR IS declared, so the rule still executes and still fires. That is the whole point of pairing this with the all-absent scenario: Any moves the verdict ONLY when EVERY listed column is absent, and if it ever moved on a single absence this file would go SKIPPED and RED. Mirrors cdisc/CDISC-CG0328-invalid_teenrl_absent-TE, whose Check, Scope and Output_Variables are byte-identical to this rule's."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=2 ETCD=TRT TEDUR=
dataset TE label="Trial Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
col TESTRL  type=Char label="Rule for Start of Element"
col TEDUR   type=Char label="Planned Duration of Element"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TE | SCRN | Screening | Informed consent | P14D
CDISCPILOT01 | TE | TRT  | Treatment | First dose       |
